{
  "case_id": "2010-10-179",
  "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Chief Justice Roberts: We'll now hear argument in Case 10-179, Stern v. Marshall."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kent L. Richland",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0000-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He alleged he was damaged because she falsely accused him of cheating her out of money that her late husband intended to give her."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kent L. Richland",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court's cases established that the bankruptcy court was constitutionally authorized to decide that entire dispute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What's the authority at all for a bankruptcy court to adjudicate proof of claims, without violating Article III?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0000-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I -- I'd like to begin by addressing Justice Scalia's question about the -- what's sometimes referred to as the unconstitutional conditions doctrine, whether it's appropriate to place a person in a position where he has to make a choice whether to assert one of two constitutional rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0000-0007",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the idea that the Respondent in this case has a right to an Article III tribunal and should not likely be held to have waived it, I think that a person who seeks affirmative relief from a court doesn't waive all his constitutional rights, to be sure, but should ordinarily be taken to accept the consequences that ordinarily follow from a request for judicial relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A State can do that, but can the Federal Government make it the price that you pay for -- for going into a non-Article III tribunal?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent cites no contrary authority from this Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Will you include in that this 157(b)(5), because this whole thing would be a futile exercise if that tort claim comes -- comes out of the bankruptcy judge's -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are three possible grounds for affirmance of the Ninth Circuit in this case, one constitutional and two statutory; and the 157(b)(5) ground which was preserved below received some discussion at the very end of Mr. Stewart's argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0001-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Parallel reasoning is unavailable in the context of bankruptcy proceedings because creditors lack an alternative forum to the bankruptcy court in which to pursue their claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: In which case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Englert",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ENGLERT: Well, I'm not saying Marathon makes this case a slam-dunk for me, Justice Breyer. I am saying Marathon rejects many, if not all, of the premises of your question, starting with -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Englert",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ENGLERT: I -- I don't have a case count for you, Justice Scalia. Some did, I must concede that some did, but certainly not all did."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Judge Keller",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Judge Keller granted the motion to withdraw the reference."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-10-179",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86820512e180-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: If -- if we were to decide this case, and suppose we decide every other question and suppose you lost, then wouldn't we send it back for you -- if you're right on that, for the Ninth Circuit to decide about that as an independent basis for no jurisdiction?"
    },
    {
